isabling host name verification leaves your application potentially vulnerable to Man-in-the-Middle attacks and should only be done with the utmost care typically only in a development / testing environment. Never disable host name verification in production or in a scenario where you are making remote calls over the internet."],"additions":10,"deletions":3,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/main/docs/guide/httpServer/serverConfiguration/https.adoc","lines":["@@ -148,3 +148,20 @@ Start Micronaut, and the application will run on `https://localhost:8443` using"," Keeping HTTPS certificates up-to-date after expiry can be a challenge. A great solution to this is https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Automated_Certificate_Management_Environment[Automated Certificate Management Environment] (ACME) and the https://micronaut-projects.github.io/micronaut-acme/latest/guide/index.html[Micronaut ACME Module] which provides support for automatically refreshing certificates from a certificate authority."," "," If the use of a certificate authority is not possible, and you need to manually update certificates from disk then you should use the <<certificates, file-based certificate provider>>. As long as the underlying file system supports file watching, the provider will automatically recognize an updated key or certificate file.","+","+== Serving with a Provided SSLContext","+","+When the key and trust material are managed elsewhere, the server can serve with a ready `javax.net.ssl.SSLContext` bean instead. Name the bean with `context-name`; the client authentication mode, protocols and ciphers still apply, and ALPN is negotiated for HTTP/2:","+","+.Provided SSLContext Configuration Example","+[configuration]","+----","+micronaut:","+  server:","+    ssl:","+      enabled: true","+      context-name: mtls","+      client-authentication: need","+----","+","+A context set programmatically with `ServerSslConfiguration.setSslContext(..)` takes precedence over `context-name`. A provided context cannot be used for HTTP/3.",""],"additions":17,"deletions":0,"truncated":false}],"additions":372,"deletions":12,"truncated":false,"file_count":10},"error":null,"fetched_at":"2026-10-18T13:01:01.869313+00:00"}